Video: VideoAV1EncodeDecodeInfoDesc::keyFrame, and D3D12 describes the frame from its metadata.

GetVideoAV1EncodeDecodeInfo on D3D12 parses encodedPayloadHeader as OBUs when one is given, but the
D3D12 encoder writes tile data only, so the parse fails and the call answers FAILURE without a
message, while Vulkan requires the header. And D3D12 decides the frame is inter whenever references
are given: the metadata carries no frame type, so a key frame described with the caller's reference
snapshot comes back as P. Since 39ce136.

This makes D3D12 describe the frame from the encoder's metadata whether a header is given or not, so
the same call works on both backends, and adds VideoAV1EncodeDecodeInfoDesc::keyFrame, optional and
false by default: set, the references are not used. Vulkan reads the frame type from the OBUs.
Measured on v190, NVIDIA, Agility 1.619: with the payload's first bytes as the header, FAILURE and
no message; with two agreeing references for a key frame, frame type P. With the change, the header
case describes the frame exactly as without the header (IDR, 22 bytes, q index 40), keyFrame with
the same references describes an IDR frame, and without keyFrame they still make it P.

diff --git a/Include/Extensions/NRIVideo.h b/Include/Extensions/NRIVideo.h
index a9b39eb..fa3d4db 100644
--- a/Include/Extensions/NRIVideo.h
+++ b/Include/Extensions/NRIVideo.h
@@ -885,10 +885,11 @@ NriStruct(VideoEncodeFeedback) {
 NriStruct(VideoAV1EncodeDecodeInfoDesc) {
     const NriPtr(VideoEncodeFeedback) feedback;
     const NriPtr(VideoAV1SequenceDesc) sequence;
-    NriOptional const uint8_t* encodedPayloadHeader; // first bytes of the encoded payload; returned bitstream ranges are bounded by "feedback"
+    NriOptional const uint8_t* encodedPayloadHeader; // first bytes of the encoded payload; returned bitstream ranges are bounded by "feedback" (VK: required, D3D12: not read, the encoder writes no OBUs and its metadata describes the frame)
     uint64_t encodedPayloadHeaderSize;
     NriOptional const NriPtr(VideoAV1ReferenceDesc) references; // previous AV1 DPB snapshot; required for inter frames
     NriOptional uint32_t referenceNum;
+    NriOptional bool keyFrame; // the frame was encoded as a key frame: "references" are not used (D3D12 can't tell it from the encoder's metadata)
 };
 
 NriStruct(VideoAV1EncodeDecodeInfo) {
